{
  "format_version": 2,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Getting started with Mars (R)",
    "language": "r"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Getting started with Mars (R)\n\n**Mars** is an interactive notebook where code cells share a persistent R\nsession. A `.mars` notebook is a JSON document made of **markdown**,\n**code**, and **raw** cells. Code cells run from top to bottom in a shared\nglobal environment, so bindings created in one cell are available in every\nlater cell — like an R session or RStudio, but with Mars's own document\nformat and kernel.\n\nThis notebook is a tour of the R basics: vectors and factors, matrices and\ndata frames, vectorized operations, control flow, functions, lists,\nenvironments, errors, and a few standard statistics. It uses only base R\nand recommended packages (`stats`, `utils`), so it runs anywhere `Rscript`\nis installed.\n\n> Tip: R is vectorized — prefer operating on whole vectors over loops.\n> Assignment is `<-` (or `=`); `->` assigns right-to-left.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "how-notebooks-work",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## How a notebook works\n\n| Cell type | Purpose |\n| --------- | ------- |\n| `markdown` | Explanations, headings, lists, tables, links, and code snippets |\n| `code` | R source executed in a shared global environment |\n| `raw` | Text preserved verbatim, without rendering or execution |\n\nWhen a code cell runs:\n\n1. Mars sends the source to the R driver.\n2. The driver parses it and evaluates each top-level expression in order.\n3. `stdout`/`stderr` stream live; the trailing visible expression's value\n   prints like the REPL (via `print`/`str`-style output).\n4. Errors are reported as cell errors and do not stop later cells — fix the\n   cell and re-run it.\n\n`ans` holds the last printed value.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "markdown-essentials",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Markdown essentials\n\nMarkdown cells support **bold**, *italic*, ~~strikethrough~~, `inline code`,\n[links](https://github.com/hieudoanm/mars), lists, tables, block quotes, and\nfenced code blocks.\n\n- unordered list item\n- another item\n  - nested item\n\n1. ordered item\n2. another item\n\n```r\nnumbers <- c(1, 2, 3)\nsum(numbers)\n```\n\n> Block quotes are great for callouts.\n\n| Feature | Supported |\n| ------- | --------- |\n| Headings | yes |\n| Tables | yes |\n| LaTeX | `$E = mc^2$` |",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "raw-cell",
      "cell_type": "raw",
      "source": "A raw cell is stored and exported verbatim.\nIt is useful for generated text or content that should not be parsed.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "first-code-cell",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Your first code cell\n\nThe next cell defines a tiny `report()` helper that prints labelled output.\nIt stays available to every later cell, just like a function defined at the\ntop of a script.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "setup-report",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "report <- function(title, ...) {\n  cat(title, \"\\n\", sep = \"\")\n  for (line in list(...)) cat(\"  \", line, \"\\n\", sep = \"\")\n}\n\nreport(\"Mars R kernel is alive\", \"R\", \"shared session\")",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "values-types",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Values and types\n\nR is vectorized: almost everything is a vector. The atomic vector types are\n`logical`, `integer`, `double` (numeric), `character`, and `complex`, plus\n`raw` bytes and `list` for heterogeneous data. Scalars are length-1\nvectors.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "values",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "language <- \"R\"\nyear <- 2026L\npi <- 3.141592653589793\nis_fun <- TRUE\nnothing <- NULL\n\nreport(\n  \"values\",\n  paste0(\"language = \", language, \" (\", typeof(language), \")\"),\n  paste0(\"year = \", year, \" (\", typeof(year), \")\"),\n  paste0(\"pi = \", pi, \" (\", typeof(pi), \")\"),\n  paste0(\"is_fun = \", is_fun, \" (\", typeof(is_fun), \")\"),\n  paste0(\"nothing = \", ifelse(is.null(nothing), \"NULL\", \"not NULL\"), \" (\", typeof(nothing), \")\"),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vectors",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vectors\n\n`c()` combines values into a vector; `:` makes sequences; `seq()` and\n`rep()` build vectors too. `length()` gives size, `names()` labels\nelements.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vectors-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "numbers <- c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\nevens <- seq(2, 10, by = 2)\nrepeated <- rep(c(\"a\", \"b\"), times = 2)\nletters_named <- c(first = 1, second = 2)\n\nreport(\n  \"vectors\",\n  paste0(\"numbers = \", paste(numbers, collapse = \", \"), \" length = \", length(numbers)),\n  paste0(\"evens = \", paste(evens, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"repeated = \", paste(repeated, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"names(letters_named) = \", paste(names(letters_named), collapse = \", \")),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vectorization",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Vectorized arithmetic\n\nR's superpower: arithmetic and most functions operate elementwise on\nvectors automatically. `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `^`, `%%`, and comparisons all\nvectorize; `sum()`, `mean()`, `max()` reduce.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vectorized-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "a <- 17\nb <- 5\nxs <- c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)\nys <- c(10, 20, 30, 40, 50)\n\nreport(\n  \"vectorized arithmetic\",\n  paste0(a, \" + \", b, \" = \", a + b),\n  paste0(a, \" / \", b, \" = \", a / b),\n  paste0(a, \" %% \", b, \" = \", a %% b, \" (remainder)\"),\n  paste0(a, \" ^ \", b, \" = \", a ^ b),\n  paste0(\"xs + ys = \", paste(xs + ys, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"xs * 2 = \", paste(xs * 2, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"xs > 3 = \", paste(xs > 3, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"sum(xs) = \", sum(xs), \", mean(xs) = \", mean(xs)),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "indexing-subsetting",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Indexing and subsetting\n\nR indexing is 1-based. `x[i]` selects, `x[-i]` excludes, `x[a:b]` slices,\n`x[cond]` filters by a logical vector, and `x[\"name\"]` selects by name.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "indexing-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "v <- c(10, 20, 30, 40, 50)\nnamed <- c(alpha = 1, beta = 2, gamma = 3)\n\nreport(\n  \"indexing\",\n  paste0(\"v[1] = \", v[1], \" (first element)\"),\n  paste0(\"v[2:4] = \", paste(v[2:4], collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"v[-1] = \", paste(v[-1], collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"v[v > 25] = \", paste(v[v > 25], collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"named[\"beta\"] = \", named[\"beta\"]),\n  paste0(\"which(v == 30) = \", which(v == 30)),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "strings",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Strings\n\nCharacter vectors hold text. `paste()`/`paste0()` concatenate, `sprintf()`\nformats, `nchar()`/`substr()`/`grepl()` inspect, and `strsplit()` splits.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "strings-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "name <- \"mars\"\nshout <- toupper(name)\nslug <- gsub(\" \", \"-\", tolower(shout))\nwords <- strsplit(\"interactive notebooks are fun\", \" \")[[1]]\njoined <- paste(words, collapse = \" | \")\n\nreport(\n  \"strings\",\n  paste0(\"name = \", sQuote(name)),\n  paste0(\"shout = \", shout),\n  paste0(\"slug = \", slug),\n  paste0(\"words = \", paste(words, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"joined = \", sQuote(joined)),\n  paste0(\"nchar(joined) = \", nchar(joined)),\n  paste0(\"substr(joined, 1, 10) = \", substr(joined, 1, 10)),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "factors",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Factors\n\n`factor()` encodes categorical data as levels — the foundation of R's\nstatistical modelling. `levels()`, `table()`, and `reorder()` work with\nthem.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "factors-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "sizes <- factor(c(\"S\", \"M\", \"L\", \"M\", \"S\", \"L\"), levels = c(\"S\", \"M\", \"L\"))\ncolors <- factor(c(\"red\", \"blue\", \"red\", \"green\"))\n\nreport(\n  \"factors\",\n  paste0(\"sizes = \", paste(as.character(sizes), collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"levels(sizes) = \", paste(levels(sizes), collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"table(sizes) = \", paste(names(table(sizes)), table(sizes), sep = \":\", collapse = \" \")),\n  paste0(\"colors = \", paste(as.character(colors), collapse = \", \")),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "matrices-arrays",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Matrices and arrays\n\n`matrix()` builds 2-D arrays; `array()` builds N-D. `dim()` sets/reads\ndimensions, `t()` transposes, `%*%` multiplies, and `[i, j]` indexes.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "matrices-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "m <- matrix(1:6, nrow = 2)\ncolnames(m) <- c(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\")\ntranspose <- t(m)\nproduct <- m %*% t(m)\narr <- array(1:8, dim = c(2, 2, 2))\n\nreport(\n  \"matrices\",\n  paste0(\"m[1,] = \", paste(m[1, ], collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"m[,\"b\"] = \", paste(m[, \"b\"], collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"t(m)[1,] = \", paste(transpose[1, ], collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"m %*% t(m) = \", paste(as.vector(product), collapse = \" \")),\n  paste0(\"dim(arr) = \", paste(dim(arr), collapse = \"x\")),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "data-frames",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Data frames\n\n`data.frame()` is R's table type — a named list of equal-length vectors.\n`$` and `[[\"name\"]]` access columns, `[rows, cols]` subsets, and\n`str()`/`summary()` inspect.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "dataframes-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "df <- data.frame(\n  name = c(\"alpha\", \"beta\", \"gamma\"),\n  score = c(87, 92, 78),\n  passed = c(TRUE, TRUE, FALSE),\n  stringsAsFactors = FALSE\n)\n\nreport(\n  \"data frames\",\n  paste0(\"nrow(df) = \", nrow(df), \", ncol(df) = \", ncol(df)),\n  paste0(\"df$score = \", paste(df$score, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"df[df$score > 80, \"name\"] = \", paste(df[df$score > 80, \"name\"], collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"mean(df$score) = \", round(mean(df$score), 2)),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "control-flow",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Control flow\n\n`if`/`else if`/`else`, `for`, `while`, and `repeat` cover branching and\niteration. R's `if` returns a value, so `x <- if (cond) a else b` works.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "control-flow-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "grade <- function(s) {\n  if (s >= 90) \"A\"\n  else if (s >= 80) \"B\"\n  else if (s >= 70) \"C\"\n  else \"F\"\n}\n\nscore <- 87\ncount <- 0\nwhile (count < 3) {\n  count <- count + 1\n}\nlabel <- if (score >= 60) \"pass\" else \"fail\"\n\nreport(\n  \"control flow\",\n  paste0(\"grade(\", score, \") = \", grade(score)),\n  paste0(\"while loop ran \", count, \" times\"),\n  paste0(\"label = \", label),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "apply-family",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The apply family\n\n`lapply()`/`sapply()` map functions over lists/vectors, `vapply()` is the\ntyped version, `mapply()` iterates over multiple vectors, and\n`tapply()`/`aggregate()` summarise by group.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "apply-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "words <- c(\"alpha\", \"beta\", \"gamma\", \"delta\")\nsquares <- sapply(1:5, function(x) x^2)\nlengths <- sapply(strsplit(\"a bb ccc dddd\", \" \"), length)\ncombined <- mapply(paste, c(\"x\", \"y\"), c(\"1\", \"2\"), sep = \"-\")\n\nreport(\n  \"apply family\",\n  paste0(\"sapply squares = \", paste(squares, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"sapply lengths = \", paste(lengths, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"mapply combined = \", paste(combined, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"toupper(words) = \", paste(toupper(words), collapse = \", \")),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "functions",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Functions\n\n`function(args) { ... }` defines functions with defaults, `...` for extra\narguments, and lexical scoping. Functions are first-class objects.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "functions-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "greet <- function(name, greeting = \"Hello\", punctuation = \"!\") {\n  paste0(greeting, \", \", name, punctuation)\n}\n\napply_twice <- function(fn, value) fn(fn(value))\nshout <- function(text) toupper(text)\n\nreport(\n  \"functions\",\n  greet(\"Mars\"),\n  greet(\"Mars\", greeting = \"Hi\", punctuation = \"?\"),\n  paste0(\"apply_twice(shout, 'hey') = \", apply_twice(shout, \"hey\")),\n  paste0(\"typeof(greet) = \", typeof(greet)),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lists",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Lists\n\n`list()` is the general-purpose container: heterogeneous, named, and\nnestable. `[[i]]` extracts elements, `$name` accesses named fields,\n`lapply()` iterates.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lists-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "config <- list(language = \"r\", version = 1, kernel = \"mars\", tags = c(\"a\", \"b\"))\nmixed <- list(1, \"two\", TRUE, c(3, 4))\n\nreport(\n  \"lists\",\n  paste0(\"config$kernel = \", config$kernel),\n  paste0(\"config[[\"version\"]] = \", config[[\"version\"]]),\n  paste0(\"length(config) = \", length(config)),\n  paste0(\"mixed[[2]] = \", mixed[[2]]),\n  paste0(\"names(config) = \", paste(names(config), collapse = \", \")),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "environments",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Environments and scoping\n\nR functions have lexical scope: they see variables from where they were\n*defined*. `new.env()` creates environments, `assign()`/`get()` read and\nwrite them.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "environments-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "base <- 10\nadder <- function(x) x + base\n\nlocal_env <- new.env()\nassign(\"secret\", 42, envir = local_env)\n\nreport(\n  \"environments\",\n  paste0(\"adder(5) = \", adder(5), \" (sees base = \", base, \")\"),\n  paste0(\"get('secret', envir = local_env) = \", get(\"secret\", envir = local_env)),\n  paste0(\"exists('secret', envir = local_env) = \", exists(\"secret\", envir = local_env)),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "errors-conditions",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Errors and conditions\n\n`stop()` raises errors, `warning()` warns, `message()` informs.\n`tryCatch()` handles errors, `try()` returns try-error objects, and\n`withCallingHandlers()` catches conditions.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "errors-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "parse_int <- function(text) {\n  tryCatch(\n    {\n      value <- suppressWarnings(as.integer(text))\n      if (is.na(value)) stop(\"not an integer\")\n      value\n    },\n    error = function(e) paste0(\"not a number: \", conditionMessage(e))\n  )\n}\n\nresults <- sapply(c(\"42\", \"3.14\", \"mars\", \"\"), parse_int)\n\nreport(\n  \"errors\",\n  paste0(\"parse_int('42') = \", parse_int(\"42\")),\n  paste0(\"parse_int('mars') = \", parse_int(\"mars\")),\n  paste0(\"tryCatch results = \", paste(results, collapse = \" | \")),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "stats-modeling",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Statistics and modelling\n\nBase R's `stats` package does real statistics: `mean`, `sd`, `cor`,\n`t.test`, and `lm()` for linear models with `summary()`.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "stats-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "set.seed(42)\nx <- 1:20\ny <- 2 * x + rnorm(20, sd = 3)\nfit <- lm(y ~ x)\n\nreport(\n  \"statistics\",\n  paste0(\"mean(y) = \", round(mean(y), 2), \", sd(y) = \", round(sd(y), 2)),\n  paste0(\"cor(x, y) = \", round(cor(x, y), 4)),\n  paste0(\"lm slope = \", round(coef(fit)[2], 4), \" (true = 2)\"),\n  paste0(\"lm intercept = \", round(coef(fit)[1], 4)),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "packages",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Packages\n\n`library()`/`require()` load packages; `install.packages()` installs them\nfrom CRAN. Base + recommended packages (`stats`, `utils`, `datasets`,\n`graphics`, `grDevices`, `grid`, `methods`, `splines`, `tcltk`, `tools`,\n`utils`) cover most needs.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "packages-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "library(stats)\nlibrary(utils)\n\nreport(\n  \"packages\",\n  paste0(\"R.version.string = \", R.version.string),\n  paste0(\"sessionInfo()$R.version = \", sessionInfo()$R.version$version.string),\n  paste0(\"rownames(installed.packages())[1:3] = \", paste(head(rownames(installed.packages()), 3), collapse = \", \")),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "recap",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Recap\n\nYou have seen the core of R:\n\n- atomic vectors, factors, matrices, data frames, lists\n- vectorized arithmetic and subsetting\n- `if`/`for`/`while`, `lapply`/`sapply`/`mapply`\n- functions, environments, scoping\n- errors and conditions, statistics, packages\n\nEverything ran in one persistent session — variables defined early are\nstill here.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "recap-demo",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "sample <- sapply(1:5, function(n) n^2)\nreport(\n  \"recap\",\n  paste0(\"language = \", language),\n  paste0(\"sum(numbers) = \", sum(numbers)),\n  paste0(\"sample squares = \", paste(sample, collapse = \", \")),\n  paste0(\"config$kernel = \", config$kernel),\n)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "next-steps",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Next steps\n\n- **Rich output**: trailing expressions print via `print()`/`str()`; use\n  `cat()` for unadorned output.\n- **Packages**: `install.packages(\"ggplot2\")` then `library(ggplot2)` adds\n  grammar-of-graphics plotting.\n- **Interactive input**: `readline(\"prompt\")` is not supported in Mars's R\n  kernel yet — input prompts are a Python/Julia feature.\n- **Jupyter interop**: `mars import notebook.ipynb` and\n  `mars export notebook.mars ipynb` convert between formats.\n- Try the [Python](../python/01-getting-started/getting-started.mars) and\n  [Julia](../julia/julia-intro.mars) introductions, or the Rust tour in\n  `../rust/01-getting-started/`.",
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": []
    }
  ]
}
